      "content": "Immediately activate the extra cooling capacity or switch to the backup compressor if available to reverse the temperature spike on the 400kg of premium fatty tuna. Contact your logistics provider in Hokkaido to verify the spike duration and check if a rapid cold-chain interruption occurred during transit before the vessel's refrigeration unit was forced. Disposing of the batch is likely unnecessary if stabilized quickly under controlled conditions, but formal laboratory testing for quality and safety parameters (specifically seasoning levels and pH) is required before sale. Finally, inform your insurer and quality assurance team immediately to document the incident and establish a formal incident report, while continuing active cooling until the temperature is verified stable at 0°C for at least four hours.",
